NAME
     syslogd - collect log messages

SYNOPSIS
     syslogd [-n] [-f FILE]

DESCRIPTION
     syslogd reads /dev/log and writes what it is told into
     /var/log/messages, with the time, the host, the tag and the
     message. The files are rotated by a cron job.

OPTIONS
     -n         stay in the foreground
     -f FILE    write there instead

SEE ALSO
     klogd(8), logger(1), dmesg(1)
